From a623e0442e3d88ebc74adb528d8d66037c09661d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:11:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): CLI comments record an agent writer when an
 agent's process ran them [daveey]

`hermes kanban comment` hardcoded writer_kind='human', so an agent running the CLI (a chat
agent's terminal tool, execute_code, coach plugins spawned by the gateway, other harnesses)
reached the worker as "from the operator", and the ask-gate read it as David's words.

The CLI now records `agent` when the CLI process or any ancestor STARTED with an agent-harness
marker (HERMES_AGENT/AI_AGENT, which every terminal-tool shell carries, plus the worker,
delegated-child, execute_code, session, supervised-gateway and Desktop-backend identities,
CLAUDECODE). Start-time environments (/proc/<pid>/environ, KERN_PROCARGS2 via psutil) are
used, not os.environ: every hermes entrypoint setdefaults HERMES_AGENT itself, and `env -i` or
`unset` inside the agent's shell does not clear the shell's own start env.

No flag or variable asserts human. Human needs a complete walk to init with no marker; an
inconclusive walk (psutil unusable, a vanished ancestor, an unreadable non-root process, the
depth cap) records agent. Only root's unreadable process (a root real/effective/saved uid:
sshd, launchd, macOS setuid login; or a non-dumpable sshd-session whose /proc environ is
root's) is skipped, so a person's ssh or Terminal.app shell stays human while
`sudo -u <other>` can't skip past the agent's own processes. Only the places a person types `/kanban` (the CLI composer
and a gateway platform message from a non-bot author, excluding api_server/webhook payloads
and internal events) pass run_slash(human_typed=True); a programmatic run_slash gets the
ancestry check.

Markers reach the agent's own tools and leave the GUI: stdio MCP servers now inherit the
non-secret HERMES_AGENT/AI_AGENT, and both Desktop launch envs (`hermes desktop` and the
post-update relaunch) drop the agent markers so the Electron terminal pane (a person's shell)
starts clean (the backend re-advertises them itself).

Residual: a same-user process that deliberately destroys its marked ancestry (exec env -i
replacing the tool shell, daemonizing) or hands its command to a person's long-lived process
(tmux send-keys, at, ssh to another host) is evasion or a handoff, not provenance. Windows walks
end inconclusive (agent). Not covered: a dashboard-token POST that omits writer_kind is still
recorded human (follow-up card t_01a1c8058acf9d74).

Task t_01a1c7b27ca3b496 (follow-up to PR #1025 review finding 1).
